wn one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,0.5]\\times [0,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,0.5],b\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0.5,0),$ $(0.5,1),$ and $(0,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/5a/5a50d17270e3856778a32461449d1e1abe36376be549e460a8fcee9ef6ea194b.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,2i]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,i],b\\in [0,2i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(i,0),$ $(i,2i),$ and $(0,2i).$\n\n![](images/29/290a50d82323a459fbd0a790e28ff8889323cd5f08a0915f85b85a0aa0999490.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the point $(0,0):$\n\n![](images/ef/efb6d92ea0dc70fa0cbd9d82ea838b41a4eaab6ee2fc32c6fada9258a4154680.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199077 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199077 #edb/ref 1061 153383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199077 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c7652427-e5ff-5d02-9f23-39039f090aff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199077 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199078 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199078 #edb/ref 1061 153384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199078 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2190f1df-5853-5d8c-85e2-33f40f1f0f24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199078 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199079 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199079 #edb/ref 1061 153387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199079 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cd371945-c79b-5b78-9017-15c39e4d5ed7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199079 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199080 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199080 #edb/ref 1061 153388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199080 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "48b1fb46-7071-5897-9dd7-a47e1d955f6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199080 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199081 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199081 #edb/ref 1061 153392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199081 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ef01039c-9cce-558a-8067-2ffba087e848" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199081 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199082 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199082 #edb/ref 1061 153393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199082 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9ddfd97d-7a1a-59ef-8492-3fbe4088f22f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199082 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199083 #edb/ref 1061 153396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199083 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5777ec1b-f050-570f-86e4-1e7bffa77dfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199083 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199560 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that if $A$ and $B$ are sets, the Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs $(a,b)$ whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA \\times B = \\big\\{(a, b) \\: : \\: a \\in A,\\, b \\in B \\big\\}\n$$\n\nMany Cartesian products have natural representations in the Cartesian plane. The most common of these is the Cartesian product $\\mathbb R^2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbb R^2 = \\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R =  \\big\\{(x, y) \\: : \\: x,y \\in \\mathbb R \\big\\}\n$$\n\nThis infinite set contains all ordered pairs $(x,y),$ where $x$ and $y$ can be any real numbers. In other words, $\\mathbb R^2$ contains every point in the Cartesian plane! \n\n![](images/07/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png)\n\nSimilarly, the set\n\n$$\n\\mathbb R^3 = \\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R =  \\big\\{(x, y, z) \\: : \\: x,y,z \\in \\mathbb R \\big\\}\n$$\n\ndescribes every point in three-dimensional Cartesian space. \n\n![](images/e7/e74fb5948144bc61173e4de73865cb746278bd31fd87e4abf927fa01821ba936.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199560 #edb/ref 1065 8237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199560 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c18e6618-573b-5560-8d95-58ed56f05155" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199560 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199579 #edb/ref 1064 "Cartesian coordinates can also be used to visualize other Cartesian products.\n\nFor example, let's consider the following Cartesian product:\n\n$$\n\\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{R}^- = \\big\\{(x,y) \\: : \\: x\\in\\mathbb N,\\, y\\in\\mathbb R^-\\big\\}\n$$\n\nThis product contains every point in $\\mathbb R^2$ whose $x$-coordinate is a natural number and whose $y$-coordinate is a negative real number.\n\nTo visualize this Cartesian product, consider the following subset of our Cartesian product:\n\n$$\nS_1 = \\big\\{ (1,y) \\: : \\: y \\in\\mathbb{R}^- \\big\\} \\subset \\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{R}^-\n$$\n\nThis subset describes all points in the plane whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any negative real number. We can represent $S_1$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/f6/f6165f66b4149b7b2ea52a3cd686836853d85048ca890e850cb771174a150c57.png)\n\nNext, we consider the subset $S_2,$ given by\n\n$$\nS_2 = \\big\\{ (2,y) \\: : \\: y \\in\\mathbb{R}^- \\big\\} \\subset \\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{R}^-.\n$$\n\nThis subset describes all points in the plane whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any negative real number. \n\n![](images/ca/caf2299a2e8009ad5b2776ce67786fa7c7e3bdb57aacbd7df87882f59a2350e2.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $S_3, S_4, S_5,\\ldots,$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N\\times {R}^{-} & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup ⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $\\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{R}^-$ as the set of vertical rays shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/03/033c40b86bfd5cebf24d34de644f632213207386c2b67c559af7594468599e1e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199579 #edb/ref 1065 8329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199579 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1626e562-8e88-5ff3-bae3-4162438c0086" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199579 #edb/ref 1067 "Cartesian Products of Countably Infinite Sets" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199584 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's sketch a representation of the set $S= [0,1] \\times [0,1]$ in the Cartesian plane.\n\nThe Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B = \\big\\{(a,b) \\::\\: a\\in A,\\, b\\in B\\big\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS = [0,1] \\times [0, 1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\nS=\n\\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: x\\in [0,1],\\, y\\in [0,1] \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider $S_0 \\subset S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals ${\\color{red}0}$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\nS_{\\color{red}0} = \\big\\{ ({\\color{red}{0}},y) \\: : \\: y \\in [0,1]\\big\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent $S_{\\color{red}0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/1c/1cc30fcc7543bfbbf8c5c59d1436eb3b1a0799d60c9ad1d899957e8fd17d58ab.png)\n\nNow, consider a general $S_{\\color{blue}{i}} \\subset S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some ${\\color{blue}{i}} \\in [0,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\nS_{\\color{blue}{i}} = \\big\\{ ({\\color{blue}{i}},y) \\: : \\: y \\in [0,1]\\big\\}\n$$\n\nFor each ${\\color{blue}{i}} \\in [0,1],$ $S_{\\color{blue}{i}}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $({\\color{blue}{i}},0)$ to the point $({\\color{blue}{i}},1).$\n\n![](images/28/28b9aa0559635ed4090f10dd0b59f2cbb6c297f8736d9509a637b5d78d27561c.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $I = [0,1]{:}$\n\n$$\nS = \\bigcup_{{\\color{blue}i} \\in I} S_{\\color{blue}i}.\n$$\n\nAs $\\color{blue}i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following rectangle that represents the union $\\displaystyle \\bigcup_{{\\color{blue}i} \\in I} S_{\\color{blue}i}{:}$\n\n![](images/76/76ff48755dbfc3ba1943665d08aa8cfd00948bbc1ddfaab560a0af64f11bae26.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199584 #edb/ref 1065 8339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199584 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "923fb377-d694-5181-8561-c57612f15054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199584 #edb/ref 1067 "The Cartesian Product [0,1] x [0,1]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285097 #edb/ref 1080 "images/45/4535a7c6aa7fe8f358d3463b4654c735e53df373d1001916dc035290ca54f969.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285097 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285097 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "227f77c6-ffec-582e-a761-f4de9b4799f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285146 #edb/ref 1080 "images/7a/7ae3c488e60d3dcda304649e575a7d2efc54be7262a54d0455550af420c39b68.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285146 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285146 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28e4b2b6-f535-5d78-873b-29236664da4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286356 #edb/ref 1080 "images/93/9303385b85b1bedfa6add9933b1953a0cdc74581c0f69ffed4d4ad3f0a113bf1.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286356 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286356 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ab95ab01-9bf1-569d-adc3-b5dbdacd80f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286668 #edb/ref 1080 "images/c0/c0df23ec47d729f597c02acff1530dd646a6f6c506a6497a8cb4d75b7fce5e74.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286668 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286668 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cf15457c-b369-5a8b-8e09-c743087e1687" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287136 #edb/ref 1080 "images/14/146139f4429b4b864a027a263abe7a6133b5b96c48aae37d5f9bc1a3635263ea.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287136 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287136 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fff0f9f4-26ca-5cc7-9aec-5a5e9377ef1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287229 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287229 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287229 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287229 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287229 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186287136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287229 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287229 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287229 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186286668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287229 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "268413d0-7364-50bc-b648-15d4e195ccd7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287753 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287753 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181779" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287753 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287753 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=N\\times R$ in the Cartesian plane?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287753 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4fc5e64b-6205-5324-9efb-c4a7ebedcc24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287753 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=N\\times R\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a natural number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in N,\\,y\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/06/067b3b386273b09d5614f934f6525bd3e43ff46f420eb8aa7e744f635ff6d101.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/a8/a870f65350ad00d258471079a34bec49a47d331c176dc7a91b3c7aae5ae968dd.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets ${S}_{3},{S}_{4},{S}_{5},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\times N & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in N}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $R\\times N$ as the set of vertical lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/c0/c0df23ec47d729f597c02acff1530dd646a6f6c506a6497a8cb4d75b7fce5e74.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367928 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186367929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367928 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174983" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367928 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367928 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,{i}^{2}].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367928 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c924021-a1d6-52ca-a73f-6c38cfe19d10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367928 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=\\{1\\}\\times [0,{1}^{2}]=\\{(1,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/6b/6b6a47e464623fe9c572a52f7c71377136e68f41dcfd641920634b415568d7f5.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,{i}^{2}]=\\{(i,{k}^{2})\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,{i}^{2}).$ \n\n![](images/c6/c67cd0b545f0fc779d2977e38fab8164eb3b0161a18e32a615c71d88d1c30b68.png)\n\nThere are no points that lie in all sets. Therefore, the intersection of the indexed sets is $∅,$ the empty set." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367929 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367929 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367929 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367929 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367929 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367929 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367929 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367929 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186367931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367929 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2937fc19-9446-547b-b6b5-44f5115d1bb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367930 #edb/ref 1080 "images/18/186edc45b6723d68a48d4290c04bdbf9fb381f622d7684037344285c7deb66ad.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367930 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367930 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a3333ac3-c25a-538d-ad9b-0631ad7450ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367931 #edb/ref 1080 "$∅,$ the empty set" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367931 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367931 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "faff2f1e-83c7-51b6-b58d-6aec701467a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367932 #edb/ref 1080 "images/6e/6e5cb597381e0aa28cbaa19c2c8ef124be04c786543bb8488a7476f5eee32c30.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367932 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367932 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "97be09fa-bece-5e66-87e6-9fa6315b13c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367933 #edb/ref 1080 "images/0b/0b689347086db4bf406a17c633b83dbc924d4c4963a64a2ca0efa7321bd6e1b3.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367933 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367933 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8b7d5dc2-2a99-567f-a521-6bba901ee80c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367934 #edb/ref 1080 "images/f6/f63649f72c17dfc510df937118beb2c5cdc2338c9d4a7e03c2a2d495dccdbc64.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367934 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367934 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e9b7157f-08b5-598c-9e76-8f4a8bba51d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389930 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389930 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181986" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389930 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389930 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=R\\times [-1,1]$ in the Cartesian plane?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389930 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "06dc01d3-636a-5a37-9129-21c0ede89387" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389930 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=R\\times [-1,1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in [-1,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}=\\{(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/58/588f2574b1aaf0e96895816ca34bd9c6900a9b13342f44bd4104ad2bf4270bf5.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in R$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}=\\{(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,1]\\}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in R,$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $(i,-1)$ to the point $(i,1).$\n\n![](images/84/8458978c2766d899b03149de53739650932875d6463c25dd3bbde99bc6a71ea7.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $R:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nAs $i$ runs over $R,$ these line segments sweep the following bar that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/6f/6fc81e487503ce86d3bf5366e57db087484e8bd1e8bafd52738c65e8e173c387.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389931 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389931 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389931 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186389936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389931 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c16ed38f-9c2a-5692-bc66-dd955e73e0e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389932 #edb/ref 1080 "images/00/00214f8393d37e387c8d34ca2cf3a203bc59ed02243d8d1d5f66f2f7c88b129c.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389932 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389932 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bf363eee-2621-5129-b8f3-366db0513b85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389933 #edb/ref 1080 "images/d8/d8d11fb28834722dddf42c232b9734a52a0d0d438b8aea9b015f4d36d87d40e6.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389933 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389933 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "91ac1a23-682b-5c58-9824-a4ea069b0418" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389934 #edb/ref 1080 "images/16/16a277a008245ef5296a55b00a7ce45cf52b5fdd008e088ad43437f6949c4435.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389934 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389934 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f72c4674-dce2-5a79-ae01-41e6c3b8e8ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389935 #edb/ref 1080 "images/47/47b6926a31ad68d13c7e18a26d97ec6c2d173f10756e50c2e059b5dce60f876c.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389935 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389935 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e221f413-5882-56d9-8c26-c8e08bb83d5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389936 #edb/ref 1080 "images/6f/6fc81e487503ce86d3bf5366e57db087484e8bd1e8bafd52738c65e8e173c387.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389936 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389936 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ace45802-edd9-5dcf-8997-b0c6336b668d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390333 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390333 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184505" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390333 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390333 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,{i}^{3}].$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390333 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "05268f20-60a4-56fb-b13c-c24e63cbe9c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390333 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=\\{0.5\\}\\times [0,0.125]=\\{(0.5,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,0.125]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(0.5,0)$ to the point $(0.5,0.125)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3a/3a1bb7a7c54718e39df80092243a119ec8b5a6e77ec4f9d58ffb074e50191d04.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,{i}^{3}]=\\{(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,{i}^{3}]\\}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,{i}^{3}).$ \n\n![](images/47/472b6456019a5c89e585f80aa4a0dfd44f3b87c0624c10ea7b52f32e958a8c4e.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following figure that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/20/204c9a31031534ac70a599322c3f77a077440300fde2364476643c88406e34cd.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186390338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0bc74910-d822-50ea-be12-c27bbc4353b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390335 #edb/ref 1080 "images/86/86cd6fb9fd52708dd41257a7df95db869ce6638e0dde902e2f7847d09021b530.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390335 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390335 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fc5f1e81-abf5-50d0-a56a-6bbee4a28f4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390336 #edb/ref 1080 "images/3a/3a713f172fca69aa423ae4664f2a6e31